        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: توقع",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "توقع — tavaqqo — \"what one expects (to happen)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اگر نتیجہ توقع سے بہتر ہوا تو جشن منائیں گے۔ agar natījā tavaqqo se behtar huā to jashn manāeṅ ge. If the result is better than expected, we'll celebrate."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "توقع (tavaqqo) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic tawaqquʿ, \"expecting, waiting for\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
